  "number": 30,
  "meaning": "Maturity and readiness for service",
  "description": "The number thirty marks maturity and readiness for service. Priests began their service at the age of thirty (Num 4:3). David became king over Israel when he was thirty (2 Sam 5:4). Joseph was thirty when he entered Pharaoh's service (Gen 41:46). Jesus began his public ministry when he was about thirty years old (Luke 3:23). Thus, the number thirty consistently points to the time when a person is mature enough to enter their God-given calling.",
